{"compatibility":"as-is","safety_note_md":"# SafeStan Safety Note

Compatibility: as-is.

Protected data: none. The model does not condition on any top-level data variable with a sampling statement; `N` and `x` are context/configuration inputs used to construct the Gaussian-process covariance for prior predictive simulation.

Generated files: `model_safe.stan`, `data_safe.json`.

No changes were required. The only sampling statement is the built-in prior `eta ~ normal(0, 1)` for the top-level parameter `eta`, and there are no protected observations to score.
","model_safe_stan":"// Sample from a Gaussian process using Stan's built in exponentiated quadratic
// covariance function and the Cholesky parameterization of a latent-variable
// Gaussian process.  
// Fixed kernel hyperparameters: rho=1, alpha=1, sigma=sqrt(0.1)

data {
  int<lower=1> N;
  array[N] real x;
}
transformed data {
  vector[N] mu = rep_vector(0, N);
  matrix[N, N] L;
  {
    matrix[N, N] K = gp_exp_quad_cov(x, 1.0, 1.0);
    for (n in 1 : N) {
      K[n, n] = K[n, n] + 0.1;
    }
    L = cholesky_decompose(K);
  }
}
parameters {
  vector[N] eta;
}
model {
  eta ~ normal(0, 1);
}
generated quantities {
  vector[N] y;
  y = mu + L * eta;
}
